      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240560/assets/dcddc9ee6fe49965ea4f261fcb43c6f7ccd14193910e864b950745ef513e67a6.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $X \\cap Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The intersection $X \\cap Y$ consists of all the elements that are in both $X$ and $Y.$ To represent $X \\cap Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in both $X$ and $Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240560/assets/37243a3d1954c0ae7939c09ad05b6aa12a8dff8a3ae8915bbe2079051466cbcb.png)\n\nThe elements $1,$ $2,$ and $8$ are in both $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the intersection of $X$ and $Y$ is\n\n$$\nX \\cap Y = \\{ 1,2,8 \\}.\n$$",
